{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/materialize\/timeout(_:customerror:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Materialize\/timeout(_:customError:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"duration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":")? = nil) -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncSequences"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Timeout"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV","text":"SuspendingClock","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}]}],"name":"duration"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"customError"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws before the first element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"text":") when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"text":" passes between elements, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any error the upstream throws.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Throws","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"type":"text","text":") holds the one thread"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Fails if the sequence goes the given duration without producing an element, measured on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE7timeout_11customErrorAA14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutVy_x12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockVGs8DurationV_s0F0_pSgtF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO11MaterializeV","symbolKind":"method","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"platforms":[{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"Mac Cataly